user: When starting the `agent-runner` it failed to detect the currently active model, and left me with an empty choice. This is better than selecting the wrong one. However after writing the prompt and then trying to execute it, the agent model loading/switch caused a timeout. When I then prompted for the model to continue, the previous prompt was not replayed, nor was it saved in the session history. Thereby it was unfortunately lost. I'd prefer if the prompt was replayed in a situation like this, as well as saved to the session log.
Please remove the current default agent setting in the settings file, and replace that with a default provider, then allow a default model per provider, but only as fall-back when no model is active. That provider must be queried for the currently active model. If there is none, ask the user to select the model, unless there is only a single choice from that provider.
We want to reuse the active model rather than switching. In particular since switching currently causes a timeout and error on start-up. Plus it delays the start-up, and we'd rather take the agent model handling to work in the background, because it likely takes a little while before the user has written the prompt, and by then it should already be loaded. Otherwise wait at that point until the new agent model becomes available. Note that switching model takes time and we do not want timeout error, because it is not yet available. Make sure this is handled properly.
Please investigate, contemplate, and fix. Thanks

